[
    {
        "content": "<p>I've been playing around with the (excellent) grw tactic and had the following situation:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ b &lt; c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It would be ideal if <code>grw</code> made the goal <code>b ≤ c</code> instead. Is this doable? Simply marking <code>lt_of_le_of_lt'</code> as <code>@[gcongr]</code> doesn't work.</p>",
        "id": 535176135,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1755625087
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since <code>grw</code> is a rewriting tactic, it just rewrites the left hand side into the right hand side, without modifying anything else in the expression. So unfortunately it doesn't modify the strictness of the inequality. (I agree it would be nice if it did this, but I don't have a clear idea of how to implement this)</p>\n<p>There will also be the <code>gconvert</code> tactic in the future which will work as follows:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">gconvert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ b ≤ c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>To get the behaviour of <code>gconvert h</code>, you can currently use <code>revert h; gcongr</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">revert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ a &lt; b → a &lt; c</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">gcongr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ b ≤ c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This approach however only works when the shape of the hypothesis and the goal are the same. If the goal is something like <code>2 * a &lt; c</code>, then this doesn't work. In that case I would suggest using the <code>gcongr</code> tactic in combination with a <code>have</code> statement or a <code>calc</code> block:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">calc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gcongr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 535202191,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1755636988
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, I see. I guess the most natural edit to <code>grw</code> would be to try relaxing the expected new goal's relation to ≤ whenever it's &lt;. But that could be 2x slower, and also doesn't work because it involves calling <code>gcongr</code> on a goal like <code>b ≤ c → a &lt; c</code>, which is not of the required form <code>f ⋯ ~ f ⋯</code>. A possible solution is to extend <code>gcongr</code> to support goals <code>f ⋯ ~ g ⋯</code> as long as f, g have the same signature (maybe this is only useful for this specific scenario)</p>",
        "id": 535230656,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1755658811
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>anyway, seems like it's not trivial; thanks for the alternatives</p>",
        "id": 535230821,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1755658943
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, the behaviour of rewriting with strict inequalities that you had asked for is now supported, as of yesterday. As you suggested, I extended <code>gcongr</code> to support goals <code>f ⋯ ~ g ⋯</code>, and there is now the <code>@[gcongr strict]</code> tag for tagging gcongr lemmas where the conclusion has this unusual shape.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ b ≤ c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>See also <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Announcement.3A.20New.20.60grw.60.20tactic\">#mathlib4 &gt; Announcement: New &#96;grw&#96; tactic</a></p>",
        "id": 608133711,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1783113914
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hey, would it be possible to tag <code>le_antisymm</code>?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 608149023,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1783125264
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure what you mean. Recall that <code>grw [a, b]</code> is just shorthand for <code>grw [a]; grw[b]</code>, just like in <code>rw</code>. What do you expect from this?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 608173027,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1783150740
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/grw.3A.20more.20useful.20handling.20of.20.3C.2F.E2.89.A4.3F/near/608133711\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>See also <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Announcement.3A.20New.20.60grw.60.20tactic\">#mathlib4 &gt; Announcement: New &#96;grw&#96; tactic</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I saw this already — thanks for doing this!</p>",
        "id": 608176768,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1783154493
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/grw.3A.20more.20useful.20handling.20of.20.3C.2F.E2.89.A4.3F/near/608173027\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What do you expect from this?</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>To change the goal to <code>b ≤ a</code></p>",
        "id": 608196246,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1783173406
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Aha, I see. But rewriting means to replace the LHS by the RHS (or vice versa). So rewriting by <code>a ≤ b</code> means to replace <code>a</code> by <code>b</code>. So I don't see how this would be a rewriting step.</p>\n<p>It is possible to do this with a rewrite if you use <code>apply_rw</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Though <code>apply_rw [← le_antisymm h1]</code> is just equivalent to <code>apply le_antisymm h1</code> in this case.</p>",
        "id": 608196628,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1783173695
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>An example \"in the wild\":</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SimpleGraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cycleGraph</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">egirth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcyc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hlen</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cycleGraph_isContained_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">three_le_egirth</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">antisymm'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">egirth_le_length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcyc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hlen</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast_ofNat</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and it feels like I should be able to replace the last 2 lines with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">three_le_egirth</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">egirth_le_length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcyc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hlen</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast_ofNat</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>le_antisymm</code> has type <code>a ≤ b → b ≤ a → a = b</code> which looks very similar to  <code>lt_of_lt_of_le</code> which has type <code>a &lt; b → b ≤ c → a &lt; c</code>, so I expected the strict rewriting feature to work for both.</p>",
        "id": 608197275,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1783174297
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/grw.3A.20more.20useful.20handling.20of.20.3C.2F.E2.89.A4.3F/near/608196628\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But rewriting means to replace the LHS by the RHS (or vice versa). So rewriting by <code>a ≤ b</code> means to replace <code>a</code> by <code>b</code>. So I don't see how this would be a rewriting step.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think you can apply the same criticism to strict rewriting, which applies <code>lt_of_lt_of_le</code> and changes the relation.</p>",
        "id": 608197393,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1783174419
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is different with strict rewriting, because it is still a rewrite (and additionally changes the relation). But what you proposed only changes the relation, without being a rewrite.</p>",
        "id": 608197470,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1783174506
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think for such \"in the wild\" cases, the easiest and clearest proof is to simply <code>apply le_antisymm</code>, and then use <code>grw</code> in both subgoals (or fill in one subgoal immediately as you did).</p>",
        "id": 608197594,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1783174613
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/grw.3A.20more.20useful.20handling.20of.20.3C.2F.E2.89.A4.3F/near/608197470\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But what you proposed only changes the relation, without being a rewrite.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Is this a semantics issue, or does the design of <code>grw</code> not support stuff like <code>le_antisymm</code>?</p>",
        "id": 608197824,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1783174802
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, <code>grw</code> only supports rewriting. I still don't see how your proposed example rewrites <code>a</code> into <code>b</code>.</p>",
        "id": 608197905,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1783174881
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So semantics?</p>",
        "id": 608197921,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1783174907
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suppose so</p>",
        "id": 608197993,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1783174983
    }
]